# Security boundaries

- Treat every target URL, redirect, hostname and resolved IP address as untrusted input.
- Validate scope before making a request and after every redirect.
- Reject embedded URL credentials.
- Block disallowed loopback, link-local, private and special-use addresses unless an explicit local-lab policy permits them.
- Apply timeouts, response-size limits, concurrency limits and rate limits to network operations.
- Active scanning must remain disabled by default.
- Preserve the original request before applying any mutation.
- A confirmed finding requires reproducible evidence.
- Redact credentials before logging, displaying or persisting evidence.
- Automated tests must never contact public Internet targets.
- Use controlled local fixtures for all scanner integration tests.
